      ":question/problem": "![](images/ef/efa766a96b1de57f303c2cdfd80a89376b5aed8462098275c2016c21f50aed8e.png)\n\nIn the diagram, $X$ lies on the segment $YQ$. The given vectors are $\\overrightarrow{OY}=e$ and $\\overrightarrow{OQ}=g$. The lengths satisfy $YX:XQ=8:5$.\n\nExpress $\\overrightarrow{OX}$ in terms of $e$ and $g$. Fill in both coefficients, including their signs.\n\n$\\overrightarrow{OX}=$ {{field-1}} $e+$ {{field-2}} $g$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First express both endpoint vectors in the directions away from $O$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{OY}=e\\qquad \\overrightarrow{OQ}=g .\n$$\n\nTrace the path from $Y$ through $O$ to $Q$:\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{YQ}=\\overrightarrow{YO}+\\overrightarrow{OQ}=-e+g.\n$$\n\nThe ratio $YX:XQ=8:5$ gives $13$ parts in the whole segment. Thus\n\n$$\n\\overrightarrow{YX}=\\frac{8}{13}\\overrightarrow{YQ}=\\frac{8}{13}(-e+g).\n$$\n\nAdd along the path $O\\to Y\\to X$ and collect coefficients:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\overrightarrow{OX}&=\\overrightarrow{OY}+\\overrightarrow{YX}\\\\&=e+\\frac{8}{13}(-e+g)\\\\&=\\frac{5}{13}e+\\frac{8}{13}g.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
